  "name": "Question 10",
  "problem": "$\\pi $ is irrational, **and** $4$ divides $10$ **or** $16.$\n\nExpress the compound statement above in symbolic form given the following notations:\n\n- $P:\\pi \\text{\u00a0is irrational}$\n\n- $Q:4\\text{\u00a0divides\u00a0}10$\n\n- $R:4\\text{\u00a0divides\u00a0}16$",
  "worked_solution": "The word \"and\" is represented by the symbol \"$\u2227$\", while the word \"or\" is represented by the symbol \"$\u2228$\".\n\nNote that this sentence consists of two parts:\n\n- **Part 1:** $\\pi $ is irrational. This corresponds to $P.$\n\n- **Part 2:** $4$ divide to $10$ or $16.$ This corresponds to\n\n$$\n{{4\\text{\u00a0divides\u00a0}10}_{\u23df}}_{Q}\\,{{\\text{or}}_{\u23df}}_{\u2228}\\,{{4\\text{\u00a0divides\u00a0}16}_{\u23df}}_{R},\n$$\n\nthat is, $Q\u2228R.$\n\nSo, we can express the sentence as\n\n$$\n{{\\pi \\text{\u00a0is irrational}}_{\u23df}}_{P}\\,{{\\text{and}}_{\u23df}}_{\u2227}\\,{{4\\text{\u00a0divides\u00a0}10\\text{\u00a0or\u00a0}16}_{\u23df}}_{Q\\,\u2228\\,R},\n$$\n\nthat is, $P\u2227(Q\u2228R).$",
